#Problem APEX 6.1.16-17

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Techniques of integration)
## DBsection(Substitution (with trigonometric functions))
## KEYWORDS('indefinite integral')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('6.1')
## Problem1('16 17')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',                'PGML.pl',
    'parserFormulaUpToConstant.pl', 'PGcourse.pl'
);

## (a) ##
$a1 = random(2, 20, 1);
$b1 = random(2, 12, 1);

$u1 = "$a1 - $b1 x";
$f1 = "\cos($u1)";

## (b) ##
$a2 = random(2, 20, 1);
$b2 = random(2, 12, 1);

$u2 = "$a2 - $b2 x";
$f2 = "\sec^2($u2)";

#### Answers ####
$F1 = FormulaUpToConstant("-sin($u1) / $b1");
$F2 = FormulaUpToConstant("-tan($u2) / $b2");

BEGIN_PGML
Evaluate the indefinite integrals using substitution. (Use [`C`]
for the constant of integration.)

a) [``  \int [$f1] \, dx = ``] [_]{$F1}{40}

b) [``  \int [$f2] \, dx = ``] [_]{$F2}{40}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) Substitute [`u = [$u1]`].  Then [`du = -[$b1] \,dx`].

    [```
      \begin{aligned}
          \int [$f1] \, dx & = 
         \dfrac{1}{-[$b1]}\int \cos u \, du \\
        & =  -\dfrac{1}{[$b1]} \sin u + C\\
        & =  -\dfrac{\sin([$u1])}{[$b1]} + C\\
      \end{aligned}
    ```]

b) Substitute [`u = [$u2]`].  Then [`du = -[$b2] \,dx`].

    [```
      \begin{aligned}
          \int [$f2] \, dx & = 
         \dfrac{1}{[$b2]} \int \sec^2 u \, du \\
        & =  -\dfrac{1}{[$b2]}\tan u + C\\
        & =  -\dfrac{\tan([$u2])}{[$b2]} + C\\
      \end{aligned}
    ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
